[
  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186078583,
      "id": "74a902da-f299-54a3-8e93-ad2716d0e887",
      "title": "Modeling Inhibited Decay"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "8d290019-d7d9-592f-9343-ad75d92ebd3b",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "The rate at which a liquid cools is proportional to the difference between its temperature and the temperature of its surroundings. Let $T(t)$ be the temperature of the liquid in degrees Celsius, and let $t>0$ be the time in minutes. If the temperature of the surroundings is ${31}^{\u2218}\\text{C},$ which differential equation could be used to model the temperature of the liquid? Assume that $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality. Write the equation in terms of the given constant $k$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Newton's law of cooling states that the rate at which the temperature $T(t)$ of a body changes is proportional to the difference between its temperature and its surroundings. Therefore, we have the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-{T}_{S}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${T}_{S}$ is the temperature of the surroundings, and $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.\n\nIn our case, ${T}_{S}={31}^{\u2218}\\text{C},$ and we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-31).\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "a41166ab-8163-5631-9697-76206e5614e7",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "060f041b-9b64-566e-97b6-d96c231ff2a2",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "{T}^{\u2032}(t)=kT(T-31)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "ea0c3a22-c7ea-5bfd-9f33-d3972f63cb1f",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "{T}^{\u2032}(t)=-kT(T-31)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "23a00f34-d237-55bb-b6f4-46c11349d9f4",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "{T}^{\u2032}(t)=kT(T+31)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "3d968feb-3683-5579-aeb2-b352a2aa9420",
